      "notes": "omniASR_CTC_300M_v2 + LoRA (v0.3 recipe/data). ~6 CER points worse than the 1B on conversation; 1.8x faster than asr-ctc-1b-onnx-int8 on CPU and a third of the download. int8 vs torch fp32: +0.35 Amilia / +0.06 WAXAL / +0.2 snapwre CER (within noise). RAM: 1.3 GB peak for a 30 s piece with the ORT arena off (default in asr_onnx_infer.py), ~0.9 GB for 10 s. Live dictation (StreamingTranscriber logic on this ONNX, 4 A725 cores, Amilia): context_sec 2 -> 0.62 s per update, words first shown 1.3 s / final 2.9 s after spoken, stream CER 24.0; default context 5 s -> 1.5 s per update, 3.0 / 4.3 s, CER 23.2 (offline 22.0). The 1B int8 on the same cores: 3.6 s per update, 6.5 / 7.8 s, CER 16.2: too slow for live use there. Needs numpy + onnxruntime only (soundfile/scipy optional). CPU latency measured on 4 pinned Cortex-A725 cores (2.8 GHz efficiency cores of the ARM GB10, machine shared): relative only, x86 still to measure.",
